# Admin UI Design Playbook

When designing or implementing admin UI:

- Clarify style, competitors, users, and core tasks first.
- Avoid generic AI-looking mockups.
- Prefer professional business layouts over decorative card-heavy pages.
- Use clear navigation, structured content regions, readable filters, and operationally useful tables.
- In existing systems, reuse the actual shell, tabs, and list-page pattern; avoid permanent explanation banners and oversized dashboard headers.
- Avoid large titles and long descriptive text unless the product genuinely needs them.
- For enterprise mobile operations, prefer compact blue-white task screens with dense KPIs, charts/maps/progress, filters, bottom tabs, and consistent status colors.

## Cross-Project Standards

新项目启动、设计系统制定或跨页面规范统一时，先读取 `project-standards-playbook/SKILL.md` 及其适用细则；小修复按影响范围应用，保留已有确认参数。
